165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 132 0 R
/T (High-revenue listings are often assumed to be top performers. But revenue can simply reflect a higher price, not real guest demand. In this dataset, listings priced above $500 earn roughly 3.5x more revenue than those under $75, despite having about 4x lower occupancy. This project investigates whether elevated revenue actually reflects strong performance \(occupancy\) , guest satisfaction, and host quality , or whether it's just a higher price tag. The goal is to help hosts and investors tell real market success apart from price inflation.)
/E (High-revenue listings are often assumed to be top performers. But revenue can simply reflect a higher price, not real guest demand. In this dataset, listings priced above $500 earn roughly 3.5x more revenue than those under $75, despite having about 4x lower occupancy. This project investigates whether elevated revenue actually reflects strong performance \(occupancy\) , guest satisfaction, and host quality , or whether it's just a higher price tag. The goal is to help hosts and investors tell real market success apart from price inflation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
